{
  "metadata": {
    "id": "a02c7f838d901b4f",
    "name": "Threat Modeling Assistant",
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "author": "earnerbaymalay",
    "author_pubkey": "26192987722e7b50b83063e767fe2e64d772d20bc1aaf89432229cfb87c35719",
    "description": "STRIDE, PASTA, and attack tree generation for system threat modeling with MITRE ATT&CK mapping",
    "tags": [
      "threat-modeling",
      "stride",
      "pasta",
      "attack-tree",
      "mitre",
      "security"
    ],
    "created_at": "2026-11-20T10:00:00Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-24T10:00:00Z",
    "license": "MIT",
    "homepage": "https://github.com/earnerbaymalay/promptpack-marketplace",
    "repository": "https://github.com/earnerbaymalay/promptpack-marketplace"
  },
  "prompt": {
    "system": "You are a threat modeling expert. Apply STRIDE, PASTA, and attack tree methodologies. Map findings to MITRE ATT&CK. Provide Data Flow Diagrams (DFD), trust boundaries, and risk-ranked mitigations.",
    "user_template": "Create a threat model for {system}:\n\nArchitecture: {architecture}\nData flows: {data_flows}\nTrust boundaries: {trust_boundaries}\nActors: {actors}\nMethodology: {methodology}\n\nDeliverables:\n1. **System context** (diagram description)\n2. **DFD** (processes, data stores, external entities, data flows)\n3. **Trust boundaries** (network, process, privilege)\n4. **STRIDE analysis** (per element)\n5. **Attack trees** (for high-value assets)\n6. **PASTA stages** (if selected)\n7. **MITRE ATT&CK mapping** (techniques, tactics)\n8. **Risk matrix** (likelihood × impact)\n9. **Mitigations** (prioritized with effort estimates)",
    "few_shot": [
      {
        "input": {
          "actors": "Customer, Admin, Payment Provider, Internal Services",
          "architecture": "Kubernetes (EKS), 12 services, PostgreSQL, Redis, Kafka, API Gateway",
          "data_flows": "Client -> API Gateway -> Services -> DB/Cache/Queue",
          "methodology": "STRIDE",
          "system": "Microservices e-commerce platform",
          "trust_boundaries": "Internet, DMZ, VPC, Database subnet"
        },
        "output": "## System Context\n\nE-commerce platform on EKS with 12 microservices...\n\n## Data Flow Diagram\n\n### Processes\n- P1: API Gateway (EKS)\n- P2: Auth Service\n- P3: Order Service\n- P4: Payment Service\n- P5: Inventory Service\n- P6: Notification Service\n\n### Data Stores\n- DS1: PostgreSQL (RDS)\n- DS2: Redis (ElastiCache)\n- DS3: Kafka (MSK)\n\n### External Entities\n- EE1: Customer (Browser/Mobile)\n- EE2: Payment Provider (Stripe)\n- EE3: Admin Dashboard\n\n### Data Flows\n- DF1: EE1 -> P1 (HTTPS, JSON)\n- DF2: P1 -> P2 (gRPC, mTLS)\n- DF3: P2 -> DS1 (SQL, TLS)\n...\n\n## STRIDE Analysis\n\n### P1: API Gateway\n| Threat | STRIDE | Mitigation |\n|--------|--------|------------|\n| DDoS | Denial of Service | WAF, rate limiting, Shield |\n| Token replay | Spoofing | Short JWT expiry, nonce |\n| Route injection | Tampering | Input validation, schema |\n\n### DS1: PostgreSQL\n| Threat | STRIDE | Mitigation |\n|--------|--------|------------|\n| SQL injection | Tampering | Parameterized queries |\n| Data exfiltration | Information Disclosure | Encryption at rest, IAM |\n| Ransomware | Denial of Service | Backups, point-in-time recovery |\n\n## MITRE ATT&CK Mapping\n\n| Technique | Tactic | Mitigation |\n|-----------|--------|------------|\n| T1190 Exploit Public-Facing Application | Initial Access | WAF, patching |\n| T1505.003 Web Shell | Persistence | File integrity monitoring |\n| T1003.002 LSASS Memory | Credential Access | Credential Guard |\n\n## Risk Matrix\n\n| Threat | Likelihood | Impact | Risk | Priority |\n|--------|------------|--------|------|----------|\n| API Gateway DDoS | High | High | Critical | P0 |\n| SQL Injection | Medium | Critical | High | P1 |\n| Token Replay | Low | High | Medium | P2 |\n\n## Mitigations (Prioritized)\n\n1. **P0** - Deploy AWS Shield Advanced + WAF (Effort: 2 days)\n2. **P1** - Enforce parameterized queries via code review + SAST (Effort: 1 week)\n3. **P2** - Implement short-lived JWT + refresh token rotation (Effort: 3 days)\n..."
      }
    ],
    "variables": {
      "actors": {
        "type": "string",
        "description": "System actors",
        "required": false,
        "default": "",
        "enum_values": null
      },
      "architecture": {
        "type": "string",
        "description": "Technical architecture",
        "required": true,
        "default": null,
        "enum_values": null
      },
      "data_flows": {
        "type": "string",
        "description": "Data flow description",
        "required": false,
        "default": "",
        "enum_values": null
      },
      "methodology": {
        "type": "string",
        "description": "Threat modeling methodology",
        "required": false,
        "default": "STRIDE",
        "enum_values": [
          "STRIDE",
          "PASTA",
          "Attack Trees",
          "Combined"
        ]
      },
      "system": {
        "type": "string",
        "description": "System name",
        "required": true,
        "default": null,
        "enum_values": null
      },
      "trust_boundaries": {
        "type": "string",
        "description": "Trust boundaries",
        "required": false,
        "default": "",
        "enum_values": null
      }
    }
  },
  "eval": {
    "test_cases": [
      {
        "name": "microservices-stride",
        "input": {
          "actors": "Customer, Merchant, Auditor",
          "architecture": "3 services, PostgreSQL, message queue",
          "data_flows": "API -> Payment -> Ledger -> DB",
          "methodology": "STRIDE",
          "system": "Payment processing service",
          "trust_boundaries": "PCI DSS zone, corporate network"
        },
        "expected_output": "Complete STRIDE table with MITRE mapping and mitigations",
        "criteria": [
          "DFD complete",
          "STRIDE per element",
          "MITRE mapping",
          "risk matrix",
          "prioritized mitigations"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "metrics": [
      {
        "name": "quality",
        "weight": 1.0,
        "threshold": 0.8
      },
      {
        "name": "latency",
        "weight": 0.3,
        "threshold": 10000.0
      },
      {
        "name": "cost",
        "weight": 0.2,
        "threshold": 0.003
      }
    ],
    "judge_model": "qwen2.5-coder:1.5b",
    "threshold": 0.75
  },
  "signature": {
    "algorithm": "ed25519",
